					You keep squeaking the toy, drawing the attention of another <<childSelect _child3>><<childtype>>. Soon you have a choir of pups howling together in unison with the <<= $phase>>. <<stress -6>><<trauma -6>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>><<gharmony>>
				<<else>>
					You keep squeaking the toy, and they howl every time. Eventually one of them grabs the <<= $phase>> and runs off. It squeaks with every step. <<stress -6>><<trauma -6>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>><<gharmony>>
				<</if>>
			<<elseif random(1, 3) is 2>>
				You squeak the toy again. Instead of howling this time, the <<childtype>> watches the <<= $phase>> with wary intensity. At a third squeak, <<childhe>> snarls. You put the <<= $phase>> down. <<stress 6>><<gstress>><<gferocity>>
			<<else>>
				You squeak the <<= $phase>> again, and the <<childtype>> lets out another howl with a wag of <<childhis>> tail. For the next few minutes, <<childhe>> howls in harmony every time you squeak the toy for <<childhim>>. <<stress -6>><<trauma -6>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>><<gharmony>>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<<case "chewBone">>
		You sit next to <<childname>> and start digging alongside <<childhim>>. The dirt is hard, but you manage to make a shallow hole. <<childname>> picks up a toy bone and drops it in the hole. You sit back and watch as <<childhe>> buries it. After pushing the unearthed dirt back into the hole, <<childhe>> sits on the mound.
		<br><br>
		<<switch random(1, 2)>>
			<<case 1>>
				You move to scritch <<childhis>> ears, but <<childhe>> gives a warning growl. <<childHe>>'s clearly preoccupied with protecting <<childhis>> bone. You back away, and <<childhe>> settles down. <<gstress>><<stress 6>>
			<<default>>
				You scritch <<childhis>> ears before standing up, and <<childhe>> gives a happy bark. <<lstress>><<stress -6>>
		<</switch>>
	<<case "chewBone2">>
		<<wearProp "chewy bone">>
		<<switch random(1, 3)>>
			<<case 1>>
				You nudge the bone closer to <<childname>>. <<childHe>> stops and stares at it. You nudge it closer, and <<childhe>> chomps down on it before pulling it away. The <<childtype>> continues to gnaw on it for several minutes. <<stress -6>><<lstress>>
			<<case 2>>
				You nudge the bone closer to <<childname>>. <<childHe>> jumps with a startled yelp, then chomps down on the bone and aggressively shakes it. <<gferocity>>
			<<default>>
				You nudge the bone closer to <<childname>>. <<childHe>> chomps down on the bone and runs off with <<childhis>> tail wagging.
				<br><br>

				<<link [[Let <<childhim>> go|Wolf Children Chew Bone]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
				<br>
				<<if $leftleg isnot "bound" and $rightleg isnot "bound">>
					<<link [[Chase|Wolf Children Chew Bone]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
					<br>
				<</if>>
				<<exit>>
		<</switch>>
	<<case "chewRope">>
		<<wearProp "chewy rope">>
		You sit next to <<childname>> and grab ahold of the rope. <<childHe>> growls as you gently pull on the toy and tugs it back. You continue tugging the rope back and forth before finally letting <<childhim>> win. <<childname>> yips joyfully as <<childhe>> claims <<childhis>> prize, tail wagging with excitement.
		<br><br>
		<<childHe>> rolls onto <<childhis>> back and holds the rope with <<childhis>> <<childhands>>, chewing on it with renewed gusto. You smile as you stand back up. <<lstress>><<stress -6>>
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "playing">>
	<<case "chewRope2">>
		<<getChildrenIds `{location:"wolf_cave"}`>>
		<<set _childrenTotal to _childrenIds.length>>

		<<if $leftarm is "bound" and $rightarm is "bound">>
			You struggle to grasp the rope with your bound hands. <<childname>> watches curiously for a moment, but soon bores of watching and runs off to play elsewhere.
		<<elseif random(1, 3) is 1 and _childrenTotal gte 2 and !$worn.face.type.includes("gag")>>
			<<set _child1 to $childActivityEvent.childid>>
			<<set _childrenIds to _childrenIds.filter(childid => childid !== _child1)>>
			<<set $childActivityEvent.childid2 to _childrenIds.pluck()>>
			<<set _child2 to $childActivityEvent.childid2>>

			You pull the rope away from <<childname>>. <<childHe>> goes to jump for it, but <<childhis>> <<childsibling _child2>> jumps in and beats <<childhim>> to it.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Play with first <<childtype>>|Wolf Children Chew Rope]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
			<br>
			<<link [[Play with second <<childSelect _child2>><<childtype>>|Wolf Children Chew Rope]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
			<br>
			<<link [[Play with both|Wolf Children Chew Rope]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
			<<exit>>
		<<elseif random(1,3) is 2>>
			You pull the rope away from <<childname>>. <<childHe>> turns away, uninterested.
		<<else>>
			You pull the rope away from <<childname>>. <<childHe>> instantly jumps at it and bites down. You continue to pull, and the <<childtype>> tugs back in return. <<childHe>> gives a little growl as you tow <<childhim>> along. Soon <<childhe>> wears out and drops the rope. <<lstress>><<ltrauma>><<gferocity>><<stress -6>><<trauma -6>>
		<</if>>
	<<case "rollBall">>
		<<wearProp "chewy ball">>
		<<childname>> gives an enthusiastic bark as you pick up the ball. You gently roll it towards <<childhim>>. <<childHe>> <<= either("manages to catch it", "fumbles around with the ball", "stares at it")>> before rolling it back towards you <<if $childRecords[$childSelected.childId].species is "wolf">>with <<childhis>> snout<<else>>with <<childhis>> tiny <<childhands>><</if>>.
		<br><br>
		You pass the ball back and forth for a bit, until <<childhe>>'s tuckered out. <<childHe>> curls up around the ball and falls asleep. You pet <<childhis>> head and stand up. <<lstress>><<stress -6>>
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "sleeping">>
	<<case "rollBall2">>
		<<if $leftarm is "bound" and $rightarm is "bound">>
			You struggle to grasp the ball with your hands bound, but eventually manage to pick it up. When you attempt to throw it, it just falls to the ground. <<childname>> sniffs it, then loses interest and leaves.
		<<else>>
			<<switch random(1, 3)>>
				<<case 1>>
					<<childname>> becomes overly excited when you pick up the ball. <<childHe>> jumps up and nips your hand in an attempt to reach the toy.
					<br><br>
					You cry out in pain and drop the ball. The outburst frightens the <<childtype>>, who runs for cover. <<pain 2>><<trauma 6>><<gpain>><<gtrauma>>
				<<case 2>>
					<<childname>> jumps and tries to get the ball back, but misses. <<childHe>> watches closely as you wave the ball in front of <<childhim>>. Right as you wind up to release, <<childhe>> pounces and intercepts the ball. <<childHe>> is delighted with the little game and sinks <<childhis>> teeth into <<childhis>> prize. <<stress -6>><<trauma -6>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>><<gferocity>>
				<<default>>
					Picking up the ball instantly grabs <<childname>>'s attention. <<childHe>> watches closely as you wave the ball in front of <<childhim>>.
					<br><br>

					<<link [[Toss gently|Wolf Children Roll Ball]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
					<br>
					<<link [[Throw hard|Wolf Children Roll Ball]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
					<<exit>>
			<</switch>>
		<</if>>

	/*Hawk Specific*/
	<<case "sleepingStrokeHawk">>
		You climb into the nest with the slumbering <<childtype>> and stroke <<childhis>>
		<<if _childTotalDays lt 14>>
			tiny, pinkish feathers.
		<<else>>
			feathers.
		<</if>>
		<<childHe>> trills and pushes into your caressing hand. You spend a few moments together before rising to your feet. <<lstress>><<stress -5>>
	<<case "cuddleAndNapHawk">>
		<<npc "Great Hawk">>
		<<if $childActivityEvent.otherChildrenIds.length>>
			<<for _otherChildId range $childActivityEvent.otherChildrenIds>>
				<<childInteratedWith _otherChildId>>
				<<set $childRecords[_otherChildId].development.event to false>>
			<</for>>
			<<set _otherChildren to $childActivityEvent.otherChildrenIds.length>>
		<</if>>
		<<your_bird_text "cap">> nuzzles you as you lie down beside
		<<if _otherChildren gte 2>>
			<<bhim>>, <<childname>>, <<childrenNames $childActivityEvent.otherChildrenIds>>.
		<<elseif _otherChildren>>
			<<bhim>>, <<childname>> and <<childname $childActivityEvent.otherChildrenIds[0]>>.
		<<else>>
			<<bhim>> and <<childname>>.
		<</if>>

		<<if _otherChildren gte 2>>
			You're somehow able to fit within the large number of small bodies, and you're soon snuggled close together.
		<<elseif _otherChildren>>
			The trio adjust to make room for you, and you're soon snuggled close together.
		<<else>>
			The pair adjust to make room for you, and you're soon snuggled close together.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		You enjoy this comfortable moment for a while, before rising to your feet. <<ltiredness>><<tiredness -6>><<lstress>><<stress -5>>
	<<case "cryingHawk">>
		You sit by the <<childcry>> <<childtype>> and pull <<childhim>> into your lap. You hum, soothe, and stroke the <<childtype>>'s
		<<if _childTotalDays lt 14>>
			tiny, pinkish feathers.
		<<else>>
			feathers.
		<</if>>
		<<childname>> calms and begins to doze under your gentle attention. You gingerly place the sleeping <<childtype>> down and stand again.
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "sleeping">>
	<<case "pickUpHawk">>
		You scoop up the <<childtype>> and hold <<childhim>> close to your chest. The corners of your lips curve up into a dopey smile when you hear <<childhis>> <<if $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].features.monster is "monster">>giggles<<else>>tiny peeps and chirps<</if>>.
		<<if _childTotalDays lt 14>>
			<<childname>>'s sweet sounds make your heart flutter as you hold <<childhim>> close.
		<<else>>
			<<childname>>'s feathers tickle you as you hold <<childhim>> close.
		<</if>>
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "sleeping">>
	<<case "pretendFly">>
		You hold <<childname>> with both hands and gleefully hoist <<childhim>> up high above your head. <<childname>> looks down at you with sparkling eyes, letting <<childhis>> tiny wings take <<childhim>> on what might as well be a journey and a half in your secure grasp. You smile happily as the <<childtype>> flaps <<childhis>> wings<<if $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].features.monster is "monster">> and arms<</if>>.
		<br><br>

		One day, you recall, <<childhe>> will leave your nest and fly free. The thought makes you feel giddy and bittersweet. You hold <<childname>> close and stroke <<childhis>> small body. <<trauma -6>><<ltrauma>>
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "sleeping">>
	<<case "preen">>
		<<childname>> seems to be unable to reach feathers that have yet to separate. You take notice and scoop the <<childtype>> up. <<childname>> lets out a small chirp as you run your fingers through <<childhis>> feathers. You begin to tidy up <<childhis>> plumage, twisting interlocked tufts in your fingers to reveal soft, newly grown feathers. <<childname>> looks up at you happily, moving to poke at an idle strand of your hair with <<childhis>> <<childhand>>. You reckon this is <<childhis>> idea of grooming you. <<stress -6>><<lstress>>
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "sleeping">>
	<<case "perch">>
		You approach <<childname>>, noticing a discontented expression on <<childhis>> face. <<childHis>> eyes are locked on the tower's ledge. You're able to put two and two together, realising <<childname>> wants to go outside and hear you sing.
		<br><br>

		You pick <<childname>> up and make your way over to look down at the <<if Weather.isSnow>>moor, blanketed by snow.<<else>>green moor.<</if>>
		<<if $bird.state is "home" and ["sing","groom"].includes($bird.activity)>>
			<<npc "Great Hawk">>
			You take a seat next to <<your_bird_text>>, who looks to you and <<childname>> with surprise. A grin crosses your face as <<childname>> snuggles into your embrace.
			<br><br>

			You take a deep breath and begin to sing. A note leaves your mouth, and then another. You sing a lullaby, which your spouse joins in on. You hold <<childname>> close as you sing, each note growing more and more quiet when you see <<childhis>> eyes growing heavy. As you reach the end of your song, you hear a small <<if $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].features.monster is "monster">>"Wah!"<<else>>peep.<</if>>
			<br><br>

			<<childname>> <<if $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].features.monster is "monster">>sings<<else>>trills<</if>> a quiet mimic of your lullaby, nuzzling into your chest. The song doesn't last long before <<childhe>> has fallen asleep. You yearn for the day you'll be able to hear your child's true voice.

			<<if $monster is 1>>
				<br><br>
				"<<childname>> takes after us quickly," <<your_bird_text>> says with a hint of pride.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			You take a seat right next to the most scenic overlook of the meadow below, a grin crossing your face as <<childname>> snuggles into your embrace.
			<br><br>

			You take a deep breath and begin to sing. A note leaves your mouth, and then another. You sing a lullaby of longing, the melody carried by the breeze to the world below. You hold <<childname>> close as you sing, each note growing more and more quiet when you see <<childhis>> eyes growing heavy. As you reach the end of your song, you hear a small <<if $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].features.monster is "monster">>"Wah!"<<else>>peep<</if>>.
			<br><br>

			<<childname>> <<if $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].features.monster is "monster">>sings<<else>>trills<</if>> a quiet mimic of your lullaby, nuzzling into your chest. The song doesn't last long before <<childhe>> has fallen asleep. You yearn for the day you'll be able to hear your child's true voice.
		<</if>>
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "sleeping">>
	<<case "bathe">>
		<<wearProp "rag">>
		You notice with your sharp eyes that <<childname>> is in need of bathing. You scoop the <<childtype>> into your arms despite <<childhis>> chirps of protest, walking in the direction of the rainwater pool.
		<br><br>

		<<if $bird.upgrades.pot is 3 and getBirdBurnTime() gt 0>>
			You set <<childname>> down gently and playfully splash some water onto <<childhis>> body. <<childHe>> fusses for a moment, but the warm water quickly calms <<childhim>> down.
			<br><br>

			<<childHe>> cooperates surprisingly well, letting you scrub the day's dirt and grime from <<childhis>>
			<<if _childTotalDays lt 14>>
				tiny pink feathers. Many of them are still stuck together. You take a piece of scrap fabric and dry <<childhim>>.
			<<else>>
				feathers. You take a piece of scrap fabric and dry <<childhim>>. <<childHis>> feathers immediately poof out. You can't help but giggle. <<stress -3>><<lstress>>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			You set <<childname>> down gently and playfully splash some water onto <<childhis>> body. <<childHe>> shoots you a glare and begins to thrash around in the bath. Rivulets of water splatter over you. <<stress 3>><<gstress>>
			<br><br>

			You sigh and begin to stroke <<childhis>> plumage with one hand while you shake your other free of water. <<childname>> looks up at you, having calmed down with the gentle motion of your hand against <<childhis>> small feathers. You smile and wash <<childhim>> clean of the day's dirt and grime.
			<br><br>

			When you're done, <<childname>> is squeaky clean, albeit wet and cold. You take some scrap fabric and wrap <<childname>> into a swaddle. You hold <<childhim>> gently in your arms. <<childHe>> seems content, happy to be done with such a hectic bath. Mission accomplished.
		<</if>>
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "sleeping">>
	<<case "batheHelp">>
		You spot <<childname>> dipping <<childhis>> legs into the rainwater pool. You walk over and lift <<childhim>> up, gently placing <<childhim>> all the way into the water. <<childHe>> happily lets you scrub <<childhis>> feathers.
		<br><br>

		<<childHe>> starts to splash at the water's surface with <<childhis>> <<childhands>> and <<childgiggles>>. You can't help but crack a smile. <<stress -3>><<lstress>>
		<br><br>

		You pull <<childhim>> from the pool.
		<<if $bird.upgrades.pot is 3 and getBirdBurnTime() gt 0>>
			<<childHe>> <<if $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].features.monster is "monster">>hugs<<else>>nuzzles<</if>> you, happy with <<childhis>> warm bath.
		<<else>>
			<<childHe>> shivers, so you waste no time drying <<childhim>> off.
		<</if>>
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "sleeping">>
	<<case "swingToy">>
		/* currently unreachable. credit writer as Anonymous when properly added */
		You come up behind <<childname>> and lift <<childhim>> beneath the <<= $cmonster ? "arms," : "wings,">> setting <<childhim>> on the swing and giving it a little push. <<childHe>> <<= $cmonster ? "giggles" : "chirps">> and flaps <<childhis>> wings in excitement as <<childhe>> tries to swing higher.
		<<if _childTotalDays lt 14>>
			The wind rushes right through <<childhis>> undeveloped feathers, and you're easily able to keep control of <<childhis>> swings.
		<<else>>
			A couple times, <<childhe>> manages to catch the air with <<childhis>> wings and swing out of your reach. You worry briefly that <<childhe>> might fall, but <<childhe>> keeps <<childhis>> balance and seems all the more excited for how close <<childhe>> gets to taking flight.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<childHe>> soon grows tired, chirping softly as you pick <<childhim>> up and gently return <<childhim>> to the nest. <<ltrauma>><<trauma -6>>
		<<set $childRecords[$childActivityEvent.childid].development.activity to "sleeping">>
	<<case "preeningToy">>
		/* currently unreachable. credit writer as mochamante when properly added */
		You dangle the preening toy in front of <<childname>>, tugging gently at the fibres. Curious, the <<childtype>> hops closer, tilting <<childhis>> head to inspect it. After a few moments, you hook the toy onto the perch and step away, letting <<childhim>> engage with it at <<childhis>> own pace.
		<br><br>
		<<if _childTotalDays lte 40>>
			<<switch random(1,3)>>
				<<case 1>>
					Eventually, <<childname>> <<if $cmonster is 1>>tugs<<else>>pecks<</if>> at the toy in short bursts. <<childHe>> tentatively nibbles on the toy's soft fibres, pulling lightly at the strands before trying to preen it. <<childHis>> tiny <<= $cmonster is 1 ? "hands" : "beak">> are working diligently. You watch with pride as <<childhe>> seems to get the hang of it. <<stress -6>><<lstress>>
				<<case 2>>
					A moment later, <<childname>> hops closer and gives the toy a hesitant <<= $cmonster is 1 ? "tug." : "peck.">> <<childHe>> eventually starts preening the toy, practicing <<childhis>> grooming instincts. <<childHe>> seems content, chirping softly as <<childhe>> tugs at the toy. <<trauma -6>><<ltrauma>>
				<<default>>
					<<childname>> gives a hesitant <<= $cmonster is 1 ? "tug" : "peck">> at the toy before, then pulls on one of the dangling strands. The toy swings back, and <<childhe>> flinches, letting out a soft chirp of distress. <<childHe>> flutters away, wary of the toy. <<stress 3>><<gstress>>
			<</switch>>
		<<else>>
			<<switch random(1,4)>>
				<<case 1>>
					<<childname>> <<= either("ignores the toy completely and tries", "nibbles at it briefly before losing interest and attempting")>> to preen you instead. It tickles. <<lstress>><<ltrauma>><<stress -3>><<trauma -3>>
				<<case 2>>
					<<childname>> begins tugging at the loose fibres with <<childhis>> <<= $cmonster is 1 ? "hands," : "beak,">> mimicking preening motions. You watch as <<childhe>> grows more confident, fluffing <<childhis>> tiny feathers. <<ltrauma>><<trauma -6>>
				<<case 3>>
					<<childHe>> immediately preens the toy, chirping happily as <<childhe>> hops around it. <<childHis>> feathers puff up with contentment. <<lstress>><<stress -6>>
				<<default>>
					<<childHe>> watches intently, chirping with interest. <<childHe>> hops closer and <<= $cmonster is 1 ? "tugs" : "pecks">> at it. As <<childhe>> pulls at the threads, <<childhe>> occasionally looks to you for encouragement. <<ltrauma>><<trauma -6>>
			<</switch>>
		<</if>>
	<<default>>
		The event could not be found.<br>
		Event: $childActivityEvent.event
		Child: $childActivityEvent.childid
<</switch>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Childrens Home]]>><<unset $childActivityEvent>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Alex Children Interactions [widget]
<<widget "alex_baby_interactions">>
	<<npc "Alex">>
	<<childSelectRandom "alex_cottage">>

	<<switch random(1,5)>>
		<<case 1>>
			당신은 알렉스가 <<childname>>【을를】 들판에 데리고 나와, 다양한 식물과 작물에 대해 설명하려 애쓰는 것을 봅니다. <<childname>>【은는】 호기심 어린 눈으로 그것들을 바라봅니다. <<lstress>><<stress -6>>
			<br><br>

			<<link [[다음|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><<set $daily.farmBabyInteraction to 1>><</link>>

		<<case 2>>
			알렉스가 <<childname>>【와과】 놀아주려 하지만, <<childhe>>【은는】 알렉스 주위를 맴도는 나비에게 정신이 팔린 듯하다.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[다음|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><<set $daily.farmBabyInteraction to 1>><</link>>

		<<case 3>>
			당신은 알렉스가 들판에 누워 있고, <<childname>>【이가】 <<his>> 가슴 위에서 평화롭게 꾸벅꾸벅 조는 것을 봅니다.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[다음|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><<set $daily.farmBabyInteraction to 1>><</link>>


		<<case 4>>
			당신은 알렉스가 닭장 근처에서 <<childname>>【을를】 안고 닭들을 구경시켜 주려는 것을 봅니다. 닭 한 마리가 요란하게 울자, <<childname>>【은는】 울음을 터뜨립니다.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[달래준다 (0:01)|Alex Children Interactions Chicken]]>><<set $phase to 1>><<pass 1>><</link>>
			<br>
			<<link [[알렉스가 처리하게 둔다 (0:01)|Alex Children Interactions Chicken]]>><<set $phase to 2>><<pass 1>><</link>>

		<<case 5>>
			<<if C.npc.Alex.gender is "f">>
				당신은 알렉스가 나무 밑에 앉아 <<childname>>【을를】 품에 안고 있는 것을 봅니다. <<His>> 가슴이 드러나 있는 것으로 보아, 아마도 젖을 먹이고 있는 듯합니다.
				<br><br>

				<<link [[지켜본다 (0:10)|Alex Children Interactions Breastfeed]]>><</link>>
				<br>
				<<link [[알렉스가 끝낼 때까지 둔다 (0:01)|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><<set $daily.farmBabyInteraction to 1>><</link>>

			<<else>>
				알렉스가 <<childname>>【와과】 놀아주려 하지만, <<childhe>>【은는】 알렉스 주위를 맴도는 나비에게 정신이 팔린 듯하다.
				<br><br>

				<<link [[다음|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><<set $daily.farmBabyInteraction to 1>><</link>>
			<</if>>

	<</switch>>

<</widget>>

:: Alex Children Interactions Chicken
<<effects>>

<<if $phase is 1>>
	당신은 알렉스에게 다가가 <<childname>>【을를】 품에 안고 콧노래를 부르기 시작한다.
	<br><br>

	<<childHe>>【은는】 곧 진정하기 시작하더니 하품을 한다.
	<br><br>

	알렉스가 당신의 뺨에 키스한다. "고마워." <<he>>【이가】 웃으며 말한다. "아직도 이런 건 익숙하지가 않네."
	<br><br>

